            <ownedFunctions xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.ctx:SystemFunction"
                id="f3331f6f-3241-4bbd-bb03-0ccce7e7bf03" sid="99a496c2-c42f-41fc-857e-fa7f7092187a"
                name="[SF2.2] Acquire pilot orders" description="&lt;p>This function acquires the following pilots orders : manuel override, vertical speed, pitch demand, roll demand, yaw rate demand.&lt;/p>&#xA;">
              <outputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionOutputPort"
                  id="715308b7-862d-4527-bd35-0e94aa263f8d" sid="893d8ffb-0a14-459f-ae10-229b69535e75"
                  name="FOP 1"/>
              <outputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionOutputPort"
                  id="07f29172-1b5d-4768-b6af-914a7542a33e" sid="a40d4be4-aed2-432c-9b54-5a550ed4f5be"
                  name="FOP 2"/>
              <outputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionOutputPort"
                  id="4e0b4159-7261-4a03-bfae-f145e7411c02" sid="b94bd614-26da-48ad-a82c-cab526c49eef"
                  name="FOP 3"/>
              <outputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionOutputPort"
                  id="43edb7b1-07f5-4cf8-8436-ca37128006df" sid="95e831cd-3943-44d3-9650-8a8a06c231ef"
                  name="FOP 4"/>
              <outputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionOutputPort"
                  id="2a2c3a43-3dec-4e26-bfd6-7122d380aba0" sid="fa21376c-d575-40af-a92c-395c8e7b24d2"
                  name="FOP 5"/>
            </ownedFunctions>
            <ownedFunctions xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.ctx:SystemFunction"
                id="70c4320a-9a24-4b90-af19-d383a89e73ce" sid="79fd1a18-e41e-4fa5-9d45-cff4b6bfe612"
                name="[SF2.3] Control attitude" description="&lt;p>This function realises the closed-loop control of the drone attitude :&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>- first, the adequate attitude demand is selected (SF2.3.2), depending on AP engagement value :&amp;nbsp;IF AP engagement = &amp;quot;engaged&amp;quot;, THEN the Attitude AP values are selected ELSE the pilot consign are selected (Yaw rate demand is integrated to compute the yaw demand : SF2.3.1)&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>- then, SF2.3.3, SF2.3.4 and SF2.3.5 realise the closed-loop control of each angle (respectively pitch, roll, yaw) : they compute the requested forces related to each angle to achieve the requested positions, using the attitude position and speed measurements from SF3. Two typical control structure (see dedicated presentation)&amp;nbsp;: either a multi-variable PID loop&amp;nbsp;on both position and speed, or two imbricated PI loops on position and speed.&lt;/p>&#xA;">
              <inputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionInputPort"
                  id="464cf419-58ba-437b-80a1-3488b05ffc01" sid="1ec60335-222f-4b15-80a5-c9037e42545c"
                  name="FIP DPR"/>
              <inputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionInputPort"
                  id="3d73b0e1-64e8-480c-9128-407a4c13dc9a" sid="a7696de0-e51b-4eb7-ac21-0dd7a02bbebd"
                  name="FIP DP"/>
              <inputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionInputPort"
                  id="685a5dc1-ac95-4e5e-85da-06e45892bdd4" sid="a45741ea-4caa-428e-b703-eca3457488f8"
                  name="FIP DRR"/>
              <inputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionInputPort"
                  id="28e73f28-c805-45b7-bcd8-836ca9e9b213" sid="9ac1e775-04d5-44fb-9db4-43c752f04c02"
                  name="FIP DR"/>
              <inputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionInputPort"
                  id="c376d61a-7e7e-4950-a4a2-35a7f05efafe" sid="c4c09e1a-dec3-4e80-bc6b-d8001b0353c1"
                  name="FIP DY"/>
              <inputs xsi:type="org.polarsys.capella.core.data.fa:FunctionInputPort"
                  id="164e164e-3e97-45d7-b7bb-c9d5e750a8ef" sid="3aafc5ce-29f7-4d3b-8112-f263dad48ff1"
                  name="FIP DYR"/>
